Description: A window showing an icon the theme has in stereo is drawn once per eye on a stereo output
 KIconEngine counts each drawing of an icon the icon theme has in stereo on the application
 (_q_stereo_icons_drawn, KIconThemes 6.32.0-1+stereo3d3). The platform theme marks the widget
 window being painted at that moment (_q_stereo_icon); an item that draws itself, such as
 Kirigami's Icon, marks its own window. While a marked window is on an output that shows two eyes
 (a 3D mode, a stereo pair of outputs or anaglyph, read with the stereo layer's
 Stereo::ScreenMode), it gets _q_stereo_depth, which makes the edition's Qt draw it once per eye,
 so that each eye shows its view of the icon; on any other output the property is taken away
 again (unless something else, such as a depth style, set it), and a window that never drew such
 an icon is never touched. Only on Wayland, the route of the edition's per-eye drawing.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
